73055acd572a458d0a2e90edeedc3027c86cc917 is the first 'bad' commit
commit 73055acd572a458d0a2e90edeedc3027c86cc917
Author: John Hawthorn <john@hawthorn.email>
Date:   Thu Sep 3 10:14:59 2026 -0700

    Forbid setting ivars on Ractor shareable objects
    
    Previously we had a check that objects which were shareable, but not
    frozen on a non-main Ractor would raise an exception if instance
    variables were read. This prevented a non-main Ractor reading
    non-shareable objects.
    
    This changes the behaviour to forbid all writes to shareable objects
    (even when unfrozen). This is done by re-purposing the frozen flag on
    the object shape to reflect (FL_FROZEN || FL_SHAREABLE).
    
    With IV writes forbidden on all shareable objects whether or not they
    are frozen (with the exception of classes and modules), we can also
    remove the check against reading instance variables, since no unsafe
    instance variables can be set.
    
    [Bug #22291]

